    <tags>video editing ffmpeg abridgement</tags>
    <summary>Make short versions of a single, already edited video.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
VideoAbridge makes it easy to produce short versions of a **single, already edited** video.

It is not a general NLE and not a multi-clip editor. You open one finished cut, mark what to drop, and export a tighter cut—with optional alternate abridgements of the same source—without rebuilding the timeline from scratch.

## Features

- Markers, section delete/restore, and FFmpeg scene detection
- Multiple abridged versions of the same source
- Edit vs Preview timeline modes with LibVLC playback
- Joins (cut / crossfade) and start/end fades
- Undo/redo and automatic project cache
- Keyboard-driven editing workflow

## Requirements

This package depends on the Chocolatey `ffmpeg` package (ffmpeg and ffprobe on PATH).

## Package Parameters

* `/NoExplorerContextMenu` - Do not register the File Explorer **Abridge...** context menu for video files (registered by default).

Example: `choco install videoabridge --params="'/NoExplorerContextMenu'"`
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/icalvo/VideoAbridge/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
